      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you mean by `see the same method`? The `super_vtable_accessor` is just a pointer to the raw table so it would be about changing the super table itself. This may be possible but we have methods like `SetEmbeddedVTableEntryUnchecked` which may break this. Regarding `super_vtable_signatures`, with my change the ignored method wouldn\u0027t be part of it at all.\n\nThe existing DCHECK was there because of the rare case of a superclass implementing a method declared in an interface this class is inheriting. What that DCHECK was not expecting was two virtual methods in the same class with the same name and signature. From what I understand, what we want to do is ignore the second method as if it never existed.",
